This minimum check only runs when the code is applied. A shopper can apply BOOKWORM20 at $60, then remove a book with `DELETE /cart/items/{isbn}` (`Remove`, cart/cart.go:46-53), and still get 20% off below the $50 minimum. Check the minimum when pricing instead. `Total` (cart/cart.go:109-114) gets the discount from `Savings`, and so does the cart view (server/server.go:77), so the check fits best in `Savings`:

```go
func (c *Cart) Savings() Cents {
	subtotal := c.Subtotal()
	if c.discount == nil || subtotal < c.discount.MinSubtotal {
		return 0
	}
	return subtotal * Cents(c.discount.PercentOff) / 100
}
```

That way `Total` drops the discount as soon as the cart falls below the minimum, and puts it back if the shopper adds books again.
